# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Dev and CI files: present in git because CI needs them, but not part of the
# site. Cloudflare Pages publishes whatever is committed, so without these
# rules /_dev/e2e/*, /README.md, /package.json and /.github/* are all served
# with real content to anyone who asks. No credentials are in them — every
# secret comes from process.env or GitHub Actions — but the E2E suite maps the
# CRM API surface and names the data-cleanup endpoint's secret header, which is
# free reconnaissance. They cannot simply be .gitignored: the e2e workflow runs
# `node _dev/e2e/run.js` from the repo.
#
# partials/ is dead code — js/load-header.js fetches partials/navigation.html,
# but no page includes load-header.js, so nothing here is a runtime dependency.
# Re-check that before reviving the header-injection approach.
# Probe: this path has no file behind it. If it redirects, this _redirects
# file is live, which means the 404 rules below are being overridden by the
# static assets themselves rather than simply not deployed yet.
/zz-deploy-probe-946eb30  /en/  301

/_dev/*                /404.html  404
/.github/*             /404.html  404
/partials/*            /404.html  404
/README.md             /404.html  404
/package.json          /404.html  404
/package-lock.json     /404.html  404
/index-maintenance     /404.html  404
/index-maintenance.html  /404.html  404

